Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ShowCopilotButton is undocumented (no learn.microsoft.com page), and largely moot
; now that Copilot is an ordinary Store app - removing Microsoft.Copilot via Appx
; (see DeBloatW11.ps1) is the control that actually works on a current build.
; Disable Copilot button on taskbar
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Microsoft\Windows\CurrentVersion\Explorer\Advanced]
"ShowCopilotButton"=dword:00000000

; TurnOffWindowsCopilot is deprecated (Microsoft: "may be removed in a future
; release") and not listed past Windows 11 23H2. It is documented as User
; Configuration only - the HKLM copy below is outside documented scope and is
; likely a no-op. Kept as legacy belt-and-braces; the Appx removal is the real fix.
; Disable Copilot service for current user
[HKEY_CURRENT_USER\Software\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsCopilot]
"TurnOffWindowsCopilot"=dword:00000001

; Disable Copilot service for all users (undocumented scope - see comment above)
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Windows\WindowsCopilot]
"TurnOffWindowsCopilot"=dword:00000001
